      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787038492011,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "COMPILE-TIME\nPOLYMORPHISM\n=========================\n\n--> Compile-time\npolymorphism means the\ncompiler decides which\n    overloaded method\nshould be called at compile\ntime.\n\n--> It is mainly achieved\nthrough Method\nOverloading.\n\n--> Constructor Overloading\nis also resolved at compile\ntime,\n    but technically\nconstructors are not\nmethods and constructor\n    overloading is not itself\ncalled polymorphism in the\nsame\n    sense as method\noverloading.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "COMPILE-TIME POLYMORPHISM\n=========================\n\n--> Compile-time polymorphism means the compiler decides which\n    overloaded method should be called at compile time.\n\n--> It is mainly achieved through Method Overloading.\n\n--> Constructor Overloading is also resolved at compile time,\n    but technically constructors are not methods and constructor\n    overloading is not itself called polymorphism in the same\n    sense as method overloading.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uJXKVu5ZmmuPF5RsMOeDS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 620.4029571699784,
      "y": -577.5,
      "width": 298.6940856600432,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 240282391,
      "version": 659,
      "versionNonce": 762312825,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787038492011,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "RUNTIME POLYMORPHISM\n====================\n\n--> Using a single Parent\nclass reference, we can call\ndifferent\n    overridden versions of the\nsame method depending on\nthe\n    actual object.\n\n--> Reference type is Parent\nclass and actual object can\nbe\n    different Child classes.\n\n--> Method Overriding is\nrequired for Runtime\nPolymorphism.\n\n--> At runtime, Java decides\nwhich overridden method\nshould execute\n    based on the actual\nobject.\n\n--> Dynamic Method Dispatch\nis the mechanism Java uses to\nachieve\n    Runtime Polymorphism for\noverridden instance methods.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "RUNTIME POLYMORPHISM\n====================\n\n--> Using a single Parent class reference, we can call different\n    overridden versions of the same method depending on the\n    actual object.\n\n--> Reference type is Parent class and actual object can be\n    different Child classes.\n\n--> Method Overriding is required for Runtime Polymorphism.\n\n--> At runtime, Java decides which overridden method should execute\n    based on the actual object.\n\n--> Dynamic Method Dispatch is the mechanism Java uses to achieve\n    Runtime Polymorphism for overridden instance methods.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1xe34z3xAHBfScoOp7l6K",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 253,
      "y": 359,
      "width": 712,
      "height": 1250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 714486873,
      "version": 1561,
      "versionNonce": 1834316846,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787067636422,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "--> --> Binding is the process of connecting a method call with the\n    method implementation/body that will execute.\n\n--> Binding tells compiler on which method call which method body should\nrun . \n\n--> Java has two types of binding .\n\n1. Early binding .\n2. Late binding .\n\n1. Early Binding\n-------------------\n\n--> If child has hidden(static method) the parent class method , and\nparent reference is pointing to child class object , in this case if are\ncalling the static method then parent class method will be executed .\n\n--> Becoz static methods are related to class and not object .\n\n--> Therefore, static methods are resolved based on the\n    REFERENCE TYPE, not the actual object.\n1. Early Binding\n-------------------\n\n--> If child has hidden the parent class method , and parent reference\nis pointing to child class object , in this case if are calling the static\nmethod then parent class method will be executed .\n\n--> Becoz static methods are related to class and not object .\n\n--> Therefore, static methods are resolved based on the\n    REFERENCE TYPE, not the actual object.\n\n2. Late Binding\n-------------------\n\n-->  If Child class overrides an instance method of the Parent class,\n    and a Parent class reference is pointing to a Child class object,\n    then calling that instance method will execute the Child class\n    overridden method.\n\n--> Instance methods are associated with objects, not with\n    the class.\n\n--> Therefore, overridden instance methods are resolved at runtime\n    based on the ACTUAL OBJECT TYPE, not the REFERENCE TYPE.\n\n--> IF we are able to call child class method using parent class method\nthen this is called dynamic method dispatch .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "--> --> Binding is the process of connecting a method call with the\n    method implementation/body that will execute.\n\n--> Binding tells compiler on which method call which method body should run . \n\n--> Java has two types of binding .\n\n1. Early binding .\n2. Late binding .\n\n1. Early Binding\n-------------------\n\n--> If child has hidden(static method) the parent class method , and parent reference is pointing to child class object , in this case if are calling the static method then parent class method will be executed .\n\n--> Becoz static methods are related to class and not object .\n\n--> Therefore, static methods are resolved based on the\n    REFERENCE TYPE, not the actual object.\n1. Early Binding\n-------------------\n\n--> If child has hidden the parent class method , and parent reference is pointing to child class object , in this case if are calling the static method then parent class method will be executed .\n\n--> Becoz static methods are related to class and not object .\n\n--> Therefore, static methods are resolved based on the\n    REFERENCE TYPE, not the actual object.\n\n2. Late Binding\n-------------------\n\n-->  If Child class overrides an instance method of the Parent class,\n    and a Parent class reference is pointing to a Child class object,\n    then calling that instance method will execute the Child class\n    overridden method.\n\n--> Instance methods are associated with objects, not with\n    the class.\n\n--> Therefore, overridden instance methods are resolved at runtime\n    based on the ACTUAL OBJECT TYPE, not the REFERENCE TYPE.\n\n--> IF we are able to call child class method using parent class method then this is called dynamic method dispatch .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
